WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.140
Hey guys, I'm Ben,
and if you're watching this,

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:03.630
you just booked a call with me.

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:07.470
So I want to take a minute to explain
what we're going to cover on the call

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:10.010
and how we can use our time together.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:15.270
But first, let's talk about what's
happening in the agency world right now,

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:19.630
because running a marketing agency
is getting harder and harder,

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:21.190
and you probably know that.

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:24.970
Meta ads are getting more expensive,
and getting good results for your clients

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:26.350
actually takes more work.

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:30.250
And when results drop,
clients start asking questions.

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:31.990
Some leave, your profits get smaller,

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:35.390
and your team has to work
harder than before.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:38.430
Now, if you want to grow,
you usually need more people.

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:43.070
But more clients mean more work,
more people to manage, and higher costs.

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:44.510
So even if your agency grows,

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:48.430
running the business actually
doesn't get any easier.

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:51.170
And that's what I want
to talk about on our call.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:53.430
So you've already seen Andy
explain Tenscale,

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:56.350
so there's really no need for me
to repeat the same thing,

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:59.590
and I'd much rather
learn about your agency.

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:03.630
How many clients do you have?
How does your team manage the work?

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:06.610
How do you create new ads,
and how do you deliver?

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:10.630
And when a client starts
getting bad results, what do you do?

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:16.190
I want to understand how things work today
and where you spend most of the time.

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:19.310
Maybe you need more people
to handle the work.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:20.770
Maybe your costs are too high.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:25.270
Or maybe your team spends too much time
creating ads and managing campaigns.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:28.890
Whatever the situation is,
I want to understand it first.

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:32.250
Then we can look at whether
Tenscale makes sense for you.

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:34.560
If I think we can help,
I'll show you what will change

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:37.430
and what the first month
could actually look like.

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:40.560
And if I don't think there's a good fit,
I'll just tell you.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:44.710
There's no point in me just giving you
something you don't need.

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:49.410
But before our call,
I want you to think about one thing.

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:51.810
Let's say you get 10 new clients tomorrow.

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:57.290
Same team, same people,
same processes, same systems.

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:59.530
Can you handle the actual work?

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:02.130
Would you need to hire more people?

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:03.910
Would your costs go up?

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:06.150
Would you have to do more work yourself?

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:07.770
That's what I want you to think about,

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:09.810
because getting more clients is one thing,

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:14.050
but being able to handle them without
making the business much harder

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:16.870
is a completely different thing.

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:19.620
And if you have any questions
after watching this video,

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:22.740
just write them down
and ask them on our call.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:25.630
I'd much rather talk about
what's important to you right now

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:28.430
than just give you another presentation.

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:31.250
I look forward to speaking with you.

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:32.450
See you on the call.
